#!/usr/bin/env python3
# apply_margin_log_entry.py — fence MARGIN_LOG_ENTRY_20261016   (requires MARGIN_LOG_20261016)
#
# Margin log, part 2: record the margin AT ENTRY, not only every 5 minutes.
#
# The sampler now runs every minute. Each minute it reads every strategy's
# open legs per book (DB only — no Kite call) and compares them with what it
# last recorded:
#   ENTRY   flat → holding            margin call (from 09:17 IST — one minute
#                                     after the 09:16 entries, clear of the
#                                     opening order burst)
#   CHANGE  legs changed (adjustment, roll, one leg out)      margin call
#   CLOSED  holding → flat            zero row, NO call (until 15:29, so the
#                                     15:26 exits are seen)
#   TIMER   every 5th minute 09:20–15:25, every open book     margin call
#   MANUAL  "Sample now"
# At most 6 change calls a minute, 0.35 s apart, entries first; the rest go
# next minute (nothing is lost). Recorded legs are seeded from the DB on boot,
# so a restart does not re-record every open position as a new entry.
#
# Summary gains "At entry · median / peak" per strategy, and "Fleet at once"
# now carries each strategy's latest margin forward within the day (a CLOSED
# zeroes it), so an entry minute is part of the fleet peak and a one-strategy
# change sample no longer under-counts the rest. CSV export gains `trigger`.
# The table gets a `trigger` column (added in place; old rows count as TIMER).
#
#  REPLACE  backend/app/api/margin_log_routes.py, backend/app/api/test_margin_log.py,
#           frontend/src/components/MarginLog.jsx — only if they are still exactly
#           the MARGIN_LOG_20261016 versions (sha-checked; a hand edit aborts)
#  EDIT     backend/app/api_server.py — sampler cron */5 → every minute
#  Mirrored to desktop/src-tauri/{backend,frontend}/ when those trees exist.
#  Gates: py_compile, esbuild parse, import, the suite (37 checks, real epoch
#  clock). Any failure → every file restored.
#
# Usage: python3 apply_margin_log_entry.py [--repo PATH] [--allow-dirty] [--skip-tests]
# Run ONLY this script (the new versions are carried inside it).

